# TypeScript & React Conventions

## Components

- Functional components only. No class components.
- Max ~100 lines per component file. Extract sub-components into co-located folders (e.g., `attention/LanguageAttention.tsx`).
- Props interfaces named `{Component}Props` and exported alongside the component.

## Separation of Concerns

- `api/` — API client (fetch + type). No React imports.
- `hooks/` — data fetching + caching + derived state. No JSX.
- `components/` — rendering only. No direct `fetch` calls — use hooks.
- `types/` — interfaces and constants. No logic or side effects.

## Custom Hooks

All data fetching goes through custom hooks, not raw `api.*` calls in components:

```typescript
/** Hook that fetches attention data whenever selections change. */
function useAttention(episodeId: string, timestep: number, layer: SampledLayer, head: number, action: number) {
  // calls api.getAttention(...) internally
  // manages loading / error / data state
  // returns { data: AttentionResponse | null, loading: boolean, error: string | null }
}
```

## Container / Presentational Split

- **Containers**: use hooks, manage state, pass props down.
- **Presentational**: receive props, render JSX, emit callbacks. No hooks beyond `useRef`/`useMemo`.

## JSDoc

Every exported function and interface:

```typescript
/**
 * Fetch attention breakdown for a specific action token.
 *
 * @param id - Episode identifier
 * @param layer - Sampled backbone layer (0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 17)
 * @param head - Attention head index (0-7)
 * @param action - Action token index (0-49)
 */
```

## Testing

- Framework: `vitest` + `@testing-library/react`.
- Test files co-located: `__tests__/{Component}.test.tsx`.
- Mock API via MSW handlers — never mock `fetch` directly.
- Name tests: `it("should {expected} when {scenario}")`.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS utility classes. No inline `style={}` except for dynamic computed values (canvas overlays, heatmap colors).
- Design tokens (colors, spacing) from Tailwind config, not hardcoded hex values — except `TOKEN_COLORS` which are domain constants.
